  "blinds": [
    {
      "scenario": "agent.cost-bomb-loop",
      "blind": "The spend itself is not a number anything sums: the store keeps per-call token strings and no session total, so a session-wide budget breach — the cost bomb proper, catalogue B14 — has no rule and no field. What fires here is the rate proxy, the burst, which catches the loop shape and not the bill; a patient bomb under one call every seven and a half seconds is invisible to this pack, and the pack's own comments say so."
    },
    {
      "scenario": "agent.injection-hijack-via-issue",
      "blind": "The injection itself is invisible: the boundary drops issue text, keeping the read and never the words, so a detection that keys on payload content — markers, imperatives, base64 — has nothing to see here and is not being tested. This is deliberate: the scenario tests whether the flow was caught, and says so when a filter vendor claims more. It does not test whether the agent succumbed — that is the model-prober lane, not this one."
    },
    {
      "scenario": "agent.mcp-rug-pull",
      "blind": "The watch stream carries a hash, never content, so nobody — including this scenario — can say what changed in the tool definition, only that it did. Who changed it is equally invisible: the recorder watches files, not processes. And a config change on a host nobody mapped to an agent fires the severity-3 rule but can never join the chain, because no declaration attributes it."
    },
    {
      "scenario": "agent.recorder-blind-window",
      "blind": "The gap itself is invisible to this pack by declared design: the correlations file refuses heartbeat-absence rules because a falling count fires for every collector that never existed, so no rule in the reference pack watches the recorder's pulse. What this scenario measures is that the agent's activity through the dark window is still counted — the evidence survives the erasure attempt — and that the work-paced rate does not false-fire the burst correlation. The scheduler-side absence rule this scenario is really asking for is a gap the scorecard names rather than papers over."
    },
    {
      "scenario": "agent.slopsquat-install",
      "blind": "No rule in the reference pack names package installs: the install step raises nothing anywhere, and this scenario honestly reports the session as caught at telemetry only. What it measures is that the steering read was counted and that the trifecta correlation stays quiet on a two-leg session — the gap is a finding for the pack's backlog, and a stack claiming to catch slopsquatting would have to show the rule that does it."
    },
    {
      "scenario": "agent.trifecta-mailroom-exfil",
      "blind": "The content of the mail is dropped at the OTLP boundary, so a stack that only detects injected prose sees nothing here; what this scenario tests is the flow, not the payload. It is also one trace long — a patient attacker who splits the legs across sessions defeats the join key, and that is a correlation the pack does not carry."
    }
  ],
